    "text": "Former cricketer Shoaib Akhtar has said that while Pakistan once used to have expressive and explosive talent, over the years, cricketers have started playing for themselves, adding that a slight seam movement off the pitch is repeatedly putting the Pakistan batters in trouble. “ Halka sa seam hota hai toh musibat padh jaati hai (The ball moves a bit and they are in trouble). Rawalpindi pitch lekar nahi ghoom sakte (You can’t carry Pindi pitches everywhere),\" Akhtar said. On Tuesday, an inspired Seales led the Windies to a crushing 202-run win against Pakistan in the third and deciding ODI in Trinidad. Seales blew away the Pakistan top order en route to figures of 6/18 as the tourists were bundled out for only 92 in a chase of 295 to win.",
